      # BillionSend extension: delivers a held message to the inbox. Mail held before screening ran
      # (not_allowlisted, unauthenticated_sender, failed_auth) is screened first when screening can
      # run, and stays held when the judge scores it at 80 or more (409 held_by_screening);
      # otherwise it is never screened again. trust_sender also adds the sender to the allowlist,
      # only for mail held as not_allowlisted from a verified (external) sender. MCP connections
      # release for an agent: never mail held for prompt injection, phishing, a virus or failed
      # authentication (403 forbidden), and any other hold only once screening, run at every MCP
      # release, scores it under 80; while screening can't run, nothing is released (503
      # screening_unavailable). Not for inbox-scoped keys.
